<title>CHINA: Nam Fong down after stake sale talks end.</title>
<headline>Nam Fong down after stake sale talks end.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nam Fong International Holdings Ltd fell sharply on Tuesday after the company said that talks between its chairman and a third party regarding the sale of a stake in the company were now over.</p>
<p>The stock resumed trade after a trading suspension on Monday and was down HK$1.35 at HK$3.70.</p>
<p>Property company Nam Fong said its chairman and majority shareholder Wong Wah had been involved in preliminary talks regarding the sale of about 20 percent of the company but talks were now terminated.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6345</p>
</text>
